From c61ea9f9055b04071886d9b646d100db526fec48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:43:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] STUDIO ST-PLAY: the PLAY tab (jam pads, live recording
 with quantize, range loop, drum pads)

core/src/studio_play.c: pads play the song's scale (A B L R, X Y L2 R2) and chords (d-pad, from the song's bass
line), SELECT+START records a take (count-in of four clicks, the loop, quantize off / 1/4 / 1/8 / 1/16 decided from
song_pos_ticks, ties for held pads, Overdub / Replace, one undo step per take), the drum pads record the drum
track, a tools menu names every setting. NOTES > "Loop this bar" loops a bar while editing.
song_player.c: song_jam_on / song_jam_off / song_play_range / song_pos_note; the player struct is repacked
(GBA .bss identical). studio.c: the tab, and st_tab_state (64 B of the scene scratch, inside the bake block on
the GBA, whose pixel pool shrinks by 64 B). 24 new tests; scripts that walk the tabs get one more step.
GBA (libmgba): every PLAY window 30.0 fps; PS1 / Dreamcast toolchains not installed on this machine: core
tests, SAN and the cross-compile check only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cx71nhiXXY4Jbxr864
